{
 "title": "Effect of Rising Demand on Price",
 "lang": "en",
 "steps": [
  {
   "title": "Set Up the Market Axes",
   "say": "Let's begin by drawing the market axes, with price on the vertical axis and quantity on the horizontal axis.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "main_title",
     "x": 80,
     "y": 50,
     "text": "What Happens to Price When Demand Rises?",
     "size": 52
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "axis_p",
     "x1": 220,
     "y1": 720,
     "x2": 220,
     "y2": 190,
     "arrow": true,
     "width": 5
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_p",
     "x": 130,
     "y": 180,
     "text": "Price (P)",
     "size": 32
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "axis_q",
     "x1": 220,
     "y1": 720,
     "x2": 880,
     "y2": 720,
     "arrow": true,
     "width": 5
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_q",
     "x": 890,
     "y": 705,
     "text": "Quantity (Q)",
     "size": 32
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Initial Supply and Demand Curves",
   "say": "The upward-sloping supply curve shows sellers offer more at higher prices, while the downward-sloping demand curve reflects buyers' willingness to pay.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "curve_s",
     "x1": 300,
     "y1": 660,
     "x2": 760,
     "y2": 280,
     "color": "gray",
     "width": 5
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_s",
     "x": 775,
     "y": 265,
     "text": "Supply (S)",
     "size": 34,
     "color": "gray"
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "curve_d1",
     "x1": 300,
     "y1": 320,
     "x2": 700,
     "y2": 680,
     "color": "ink",
     "width": 5
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_d1",
     "x": 715,
     "y": 675,
     "text": "Demand (D₁)",
     "size": 34,
     "color": "ink"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Initial Equilibrium",
   "say": "Where supply and demand intersect at E₁, the market determines the initial equilibrium price P₁ and quantity Q₁.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "ellipse",
     "id": "dot_e1",
     "cx": 500,
     "cy": 500,
     "rx": 7,
     "ry": 7,
     "fill": "ink"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_e1",
     "x": 515,
     "y": 480,
     "text": "E₁",
     "size": 30
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "dash_p1",
     "x1": 500,
     "y1": 500,
     "x2": 220,
     "y2": 500,
     "color": "gray",
     "dash": true,
     "width": 3
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_p1",
     "x": 165,
     "y": 485,
     "text": "P₁",
     "size": 32
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "dash_q1",
     "x1": 500,
     "y1": 500,
     "x2": 500,
     "y2": 720,
     "color": "gray",
     "dash": true,
     "width": 3
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_q1",
     "x": 485,
     "y": 735,
     "text": "Q₁",
     "size": 32
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Demand Increases and Shifts Right",
   "say": "When demand rises, consumers want to purchase more at every price level, shifting the entire demand curve outward to D₂.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "curve_d2",
     "x1": 420,
     "y1": 320,
     "x2": 820,
     "y2": 680,
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 5
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_d2",
     "x": 835,
     "y": 675,
     "text": "Demand (D₂)",
     "size": 34,
     "color": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "arrow_shift",
     "x1": 540,
     "y1": 420,
     "x2": 630,
     "y2": 420,
     "color": "blue",
     "arrow": true,
     "width": 4
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "txt_shift",
     "x": 535,
     "y": 380,
     "text": "Demand Rises",
     "size": 28,
     "color": "blue"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "New Equilibrium Forms",
   "say": "At the original price P₁, an immediate shortage occurs. Eager buyers compete and bid prices upward until reaching equilibrium E₂.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "ellipse",
     "id": "dot_e2",
     "cx": 560,
     "cy": 445,
     "rx": 7,
     "ry": 7,
     "fill": "blue",
     "color": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_e2",
     "x": 575,
     "y": 425,
     "text": "E₂",
     "size": 30,
     "color": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "dash_p2",
     "x1": 560,
     "y1": 445,
     "x2": 220,
     "y2": 445,
     "color": "blue",
     "dash": true,
     "width": 3
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_p2",
     "x": 165,
     "y": 430,
     "text": "P₂",
     "size": 32,
     "color": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "dash_q2",
     "x1": 560,
     "y1": 445,
     "x2": 560,
     "y2": 720,
     "color": "blue",
     "dash": true,
     "width": 3
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_q2",
     "x": 545,
     "y": 735,
     "text": "Q₂",
     "size": 32,
     "color": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "arrow_p_up",
     "x1": 150,
     "y1": 490,
     "x2": 150,
     "y2": 445,
     "color": "red",
     "arrow": true,
     "width": 4
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Key Takeaways",
   "say": "In conclusion, an increase in demand creates upward pressure on price, resulting in both a higher price and a greater quantity sold.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "rect",
     "id": "panel_sum",
     "x": 980,
     "y": 210,
     "w": 540,
     "h": 440,
     "color": "ink",
     "width": 3,
     "fill": "gray"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "txt_sum_title",
     "x": 1020,
     "y": 250,
     "text": "Mechanism & Outcome",
     "size": 38,
     "underline": true
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "txt_step1",
     "x": 1020,
     "y": 315,
     "text": "1. Buyers demand more (D₁ → D₂)",
     "size": 32
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "txt_step2",
     "x": 1020,
     "y": 370,
     "text": "2. Shortage at old price P₁",
     "size": 32
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "txt_step3",
     "x": 1020,
     "y": 425,
     "text": "3. Competition bids price up",
     "size": 32
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "txt_final",
     "x": 1020,
     "y": 505,
     "text": "Result:\n• Price RISES (P₁ → P₂)\n• Quantity RISES (Q₁ → Q₂)",
     "size": 36,
     "color": "red"
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}